# Decimal subtraction with float operands

Subtracts 1.5 from 2.30 in both operand orders to verify the f32 value
converts into an exact decimal result whose sign follows the operand
order, producing 0.80 and -0.80.

>>> source
float_left: float = 1.5
decimal_left: decimal = 2.30

// Verifies the Decimal/Float conversion.
decimal_minus_float: decimal = decimal_left - float_left
print(decimal_minus_float)

// Verifies the same conversion with the operand order reversed.
float_minus_decimal: decimal = float_left - decimal_left
print(float_minus_decimal)

<<< stdout
0.80
-0.80

<<< stderr
